            <ArticleTitle>Wheel-to-rhomboid isomerization as well as nitrene transfer catalysis of ruthenium-thiolate wheels.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2419-2422</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cc09903c</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A unique ruthenium-thiolate molecular rhomboid ([square tilted open])-[Ru(SAr)2(CO)2]8, which consists of eight octahedra linked by alternate face- and vertex-sharing, was produced by isomerization of the molecular wheel (○)-[Ru(SAr)2(CO)2]8 at elevated temperature. The use of a (○)-[Ru(SAr)2(CO)2]6 wheel for catalytic aziridination of alkenes via nitrene transfer is also described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
